{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1489788-underworld-geography","id":1489788,"title":"Underworld geography","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-11T14:14:53-07:00","id":1489788,"title":"Underworld geography","content":"Wraiths underworld seems a bit confusing to me. I know there's a 'shadowlands' which is basically twilight but for CWoD. But what exactly is the tempest? Is it the shadowland equivalent of our oceans? And why are the 'dark kingdoms' always mentioned separately from the shadowlands? Are they in a separate world? If so, how do they rule over all those wraiths in the necropoli?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27062-vampires-suck","name":"VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27062_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T17:16:23-07:00","id":1489815,"title":"","content":"The Shadowland's oceans are little different from their Skinlands equivalent. The Tempest is another plane of existence. Nihils are portals that connect the Shadowlands with the Tempest. Stygia and most other Dark Kingdoms are on that level of the Underworld, Necropoli are only outposts and a relatively recent development. The way Stygia rules all those Necropoli is no different than Imperial Rome ruling all those far off provinces. Or half the world once being ruled from England. There's an expansive bureaucratic and military hierarchy in place that keeps everything connected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T23:49:03-07:00","id":1489843,"title":"","content":"Imagine the Underworld like a filled bathtub. Take a world map, cut it into confetti around cities and landmarks, and sprinkle it on the water surface- roughly in the same relative position as they were originally.<br /> The confetti is the Shadowlands.<br /> A big city on a piece of confetti is a Necropolis.<br /> The bathtub water is the Tempest.<br /> Several confetti flakes in roughly the same region are a Dark Kingdom, although this depends on what the Kingdom actually claims.<br /> Sprinkle in some <i>extra </i>confetti. This is Stygia, the Far Shores, and any Underworld landscape that has no representation in the Skinlands.<br /> <br /> Note that there are some oddities:<br /> - Some roads from the world map are still connected, even though they are on separate confetti flakes. These are Byways.<br /> - You have some flakes of the world map with nothing but real world ocean floating on the bathtub water. That's Shadowland ocean, which is distinct from the Tempest. The two are closely connected, though.<br /> - The River of Death connects all confetti pieces with each other. It's a metaphysical thing.<br /> - Usually, you have to use a portal (a Nihil) to cross from the confetti into the bathtub water and back out, but sometimes you can just walk in. It depends on the particular confetti flake.<br /> <br /> Now, our bathtub has a drain smack in the middle. Once you pull the plug, it tries to suck everything in, although the bathtub water never runs out.<br /> The drain is Oblivion.<br /> The hair and refuse that gathers on the grate of the drain is the Labyrinth.<br /> <br /> The analogy fails at this point, because some of the <i>extra </i>confetti is actually closer to the drain than others. There's a shortcut from Stygia to the Labyrinth, for example.<br /> <br /> This is all metaphorical of course, and the actual layout of the landscape is at the command of the Storyteller. They can shuffle things around pretty much as they need it for the story.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T09:51:42-07:00","id":1490140,"title":"","content":"Basically, there are three 'functional' layers to the Underworld, one inaccessible, and a possible lost extra layer. The Shadowlands are an analog to the physical world, almost exactly. Some physical features are closer to how they were in the past (relative to the present, possibly different points in the past). Necropoli are &quot;cities&quot; of the dead, created from Relic buildings and the like. Such cities usually overlap the physical living cities, and many buildings, usually the oldest, most important ones, have a presence there as well. If possible, and the being in question can leave the general area, one could theoretically travel the entire world. Shadowlands water is more 'solid' to Wraiths, so one could 'walk' on it. Byways are spiritual paths connecting various points in the Shadowlands to each other and to points in the Tempest. One layer 'below' the Shadowlands is the Tempest, a near constant storm of water and clouds, that surround safe points within it. At one time, the Tempest was much calmer, but some unknown cause changed this sometime before the founding of Stygia. The largest of those spots are called 'Dark Kingdoms' by Stygia, a realm where the dead of the Western world can exist when they no longer can survive in the Shadowlands. These other &quot;Kingdoms&quot; use different terms, and many derisively call Stygia the 'Dark Kingdom of Iron' in retaliation. Other smaller safe points are either older, less populated 'Kingdoms' or &quot;Far Shores,' more recently created 'Kingdoms' based on religion or philosophy instead of a cultural bias. The true Far Shores may or may not have been discovered, but they were places where a Wraith could work out their issues and truly move on. These Far Shores may have once been their own level, but at least part of their original function got stolen and corrupted by the Malfeans into what is now known as Harrowings in the Labyrinth. The original function of the Labyrinth is unknown, but it is now the home of Specters and the Neverborn. It lies beneath the Tempest. At the bottom of the Labyrinth lies the Maw of Oblivion, where everything goes to cease to exist. Somehow, beneath that, is the emptiness of the Abyss, never fully mentioned until Demon: The Fallen came out. This is where true demons are imprisoned. This is also the possible source of the Obtenebration discipline in Vampire, as well as other unknown things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T02:08:23-07:00","id":1490233,"title":"","content":"Aww... every time i think about the Underworld geography my brain just melt! So the tempest is not the equivalent of the sky for Stygia and the other realms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T05:04:49-07:00","id":1490244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1489788-underworld-geography?p=1490233#post1490233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aww... every time i think about the Underworld geography my brain just melt! So the tempest is not the equivalent of the sky for Stygia and the other realms?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't remember any particular description of the sky in Stygia, but I like to imagine it like a steel gray overcast on a <i>good </i>day, but with glimpses of the Tempest peeking through. For Maelstroms though, the Tempest comes for a proper visit. I imagine them going somewhat like an <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-qCvp5mo4Zo\" target=\"_blank\">emission</a> in the Stalker games.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T06:06:51-07:00","id":1490252,"title":"","content":"I think in 2nd edition there's something to the effect that Stygia is lit by the starlight of distant nihils. It was brought up in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1185697-notable-changes-in-wraith-20th/page2\">this thread</a>, though I don't know the location of the original source.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, I've used something similar to that bathtub analogy before except in an inverted soda bottle. That let me depict the Shadowlands as a map plastered to the outside of the bottle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 08-15-2022, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T02:18:03-07:00","id":1490359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Douglas Adams</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">FORD: No, No listen. Just imagine that you\u2019ve got this ebony bath, right? And it\u2019s conical.<br /> <br /> ARTHUR: Conical? What kind of bath is -<br /> <br /> FORD: No, no, shh, shhh, it\u2019s, it\u2019s, it\u2019s conical okay? So what you do, you fill it with fine white sand right? Or sugar, or anything like that. And when it\u2019s full, you pull the plug out and it all just twirls down out of the plug hole\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>I had that playing in my head when I wrote it.<br /> <br /> Umbral geography got a lot easier for me once we got to linear algebra in school.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T11:52:08-07:00","id":1490416,"title":"","content":"Ok another question: how wraiths from Shadowlands can reach the Underworld and Stygia? Is Argos the only way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T12:49:31-07:00","id":1490426,"title":"","content":"No. There are Byways through the Tempests, and Nihils can act like wormholes to other places in the Tempest. Normal wraiths do not want to go through Nihils though, that's very dangerous. Byways are a relatively safe option - they are stable paths in the Tempest. But use of Argos here can make travel on them safer.<br /> <br /> The Hierarchy also builds Tempest Ports in many Necropoli that provide openings between the Shadowlands and the Tempest. They appear as large, floating oval mirrors above byways and channels. They lead to established Byways. Tempest ports are located in a heavily guarded area of the Necropolis to make sure enemies cannot invade through them. Tempest ports give one automatic success on a Wraith\u2019s Argos roll to go there. Ports can be closed at will, unlike Nihils.<br /> <br /> The best sourcebooks to answer your questions on the geography of the Underworld is the Wraith Players Guide and Sea of Shadows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T08:24:53-07:00","id":1490615,"title":"","content":"It's worth going into what the various realms of the Underworld are thematically, because there's very little limit to what can be in the Underworld provided it is related to memory and emotion. The question is where would it be?<br /> <br /> The shadowlands are the place of fresh, coherent memories. Things that are and things that recently were. That's why they map well onto the Skinlands, because they mostly are memories of the Skinlands (with some minor alterations of emotion and perception). If the living strongly remember something or it has a strong connection to something that still exists, it belongs here. That's why Wraiths need Fetters to stay here.<br /> <br /> The Tempest is the place for memories and emotions that are untethered from the living. Anything that has become unmoored but still has presence ends up here. The majority of memories like this are small sensations or images without context, and that's what the storm is. It is a fever dream turned into a monstrous hurricane; is a roiling mass of flotsam and effluvia. I like to flavor the winds with strange memories like a waterfall of dolls heads or the spray of acid and broken glass, for that reason. Strong, unmoored memories, such as the collective perceptions of a generation, also end up here and these become the byways, islands, and other stable points. <br /> <br /> The Tempest is also the place for anything that was never part of the living world. That's why the Dark Kingdom capitals and the Far Shores are there, and were there even before the rulers lost their fetters. The Dark Kingdoms are things that never existed in the living world and the Far Shores were supposed to help Wraiths Transcend from it. Neither belongs in the Shadowlands, so they are here.<br /> <br /> The Labyrinth is the place for buried and forgotten memories. Unwanted things go here. Mostly these are the horrific, angst-laden things that people would rather forget, which is why all the Spectres and their Amphiskopoli are down here. It's not all Angst, though. Some things are buried to be preserved and these things belong here too. There's at least one area of the Labyrinth which houses wraiths (not spectres) dedicated to writing the true history of the world. That too belongs down in the depths.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T09:27:25-07:00","id":1490719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1489788-underworld-geography?p=1490252#post1490252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think in 2nd edition there's something to the effect that Stygia is lit by the starlight of distant nihils. It was brought up in <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1185697-notable-changes-in-wraith-20th/page2&amp;quot;]this</a> thread[/URL], though I don't know the location of the original source.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, I've used something similar to that bathtub analogy before except in an inverted soda bottle. That let me depict the Shadowlands as a map plastered to the outside of the bottle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the second edition indeed describes this, when saying that, if you looked to the &quot;skies&quot; of Stygia one could mistakenly believe that it were filled with stars, but in fact the &quot;stars&quot; are the nihils connecting the Tempest and the Shadowlands","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T04:16:05-07:00","id":1490863,"title":"","content":"So basically there's a shadowlands, which is more or less ghostly twilight from cofd. <br /> There are these special gates which occasionally pop up in the shadowlands called nihils.<br /> Going into one leads you into some sorta underground memory-storm -ocean thing called The tempest.<br /> Now this tempest has a bunch of stable memory(?) islands which are home to the dark kingdoms*.<br /> And beneath the tempest is the labrynth which is kinda like cofd underworld but much more maze like.<br /> And stewing beneath this labrynth is Oblivion.<br /> Did I get all that right?<br /> <br /> *how do you go back up from dark Kingdom to shadowland? Do you just stand beneath a nihil l which then sucks you up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27062-vampires-suck","name":"VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27062_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T04:49:00-07:00","id":1490865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1489788-underworld-geography?p=1490863#post1490863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So basically there's a shadowlands, which is more or less ghostly twilight from cofd.<br /> There are these special gates which occasionally pop up in the shadowlands called nihils.<br /> Going into one leads you into some sorta underground memory-storm -ocean thing called The tempest.<br /> Now this tempest has a bunch of stable memory(?) islands which are home to the dark kingdoms*.<br /> And beneath the tempest is the labrynth which is kinda like cofd underworld but much more maze like.<br /> And stewing beneath this labrynth is Oblivion.<br /> Did I get all that right?<br /> <br /> *how do you go back up from dark Kingdom to shadowland? Do you just stand beneath a nihil l which then sucks you up?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty close. The Tempest is to the Shadowlands much like the Shadowlands are to the Skinlands - an extra dimension that overlaps them. The books use terms like 'below' to signify the distance from the Skinlands, which is more confusing than helpful imo, because they aren't really directional.<br /> <br /> The Dark Kingdoms <i>are </i>Shadowlands. The Shadowlands are 'broken up' by the Tempest and 'Dark Kingdom' is just a label for a 'region' of the Shadowlands. That means if you want to move from one Necropolis to another, you would either have to go through the Tempest or use a Byway.<br /> <br /> Example: You are in the Shadowland Necropolis of Rome in the Dark Kingdom of Iron. You open a Nihil (there is an Arcanos for that) and move into the Tempest. You travel inside the Tempest until you reach your destination. You open another Nihil and emerge in the Shadowland of the Cairo Necropolis in the Dark Kingdom of Sand.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T06:03:50-07:00","id":1490871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1489788-underworld-geography?p=1490865#post1490865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's pretty close. The Tempest is to the Shadowlands much like the Shadowlands are to the Skinlands - an extra dimension that overlaps them. The books use terms like 'below' to signify the distance from the Skinlands, which is more confusing than helpful imo, because they aren't really directional.<br /> <br /> The Dark Kingdoms <i>are </i>Shadowlands. The Shadowlands are 'broken up' by the Tempest and 'Dark Kingdom' is just a label for a 'region' of the Shadowlands. That means if you want to move from one Necropolis to another, you would either have to go through the Tempest or use a Byway.<br /> <br /> Example: You are in the Shadowland Necropolis of Rome in the Dark Kingdom of Iron. You open a Nihil (there is an Arcanos for that) and move into the Tempest. You travel inside the Tempest until you reach your destination. You open another Nihil and emerge in the Shadowland of the Cairo Necropolis in the Dark Kingdom of Sand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah I get it now! Since there aren't that many people living in the countryside ir the woods, so they don't get a shadowland reflection but merely the tempest. Yeah now it makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27062-vampires-suck","name":"VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27062_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T12:51:21-07:00","id":1490913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1489788-underworld-geography?p=1490871#post1490871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah I get it now! Since there aren't that many people living in the countryside ir the woods, so they don't get a shadowland reflection but merely the tempest. Yeah now it makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one of those points that very much depends on how the ST wants to play it. Technically, you could walk in the Shadowlands from Lisbon to Beijing, but more likely than not you will be swallowed by a storm on the way and end up in the Tempest anyways. As mentioned by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> <i>Sea of Shadows</i> is a good supplement to learn about travel in the Underworld.<br /> One big advantage of Tempest travel is that it can be a major time saver, as a trip usually takes as long as 'it needs to'. The downside is that the Tempest is an incredibly hostile environment. A bit like the Nether in Minecraft, if you played that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T04:13:17-07:00","id":1490980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1489788-underworld-geography?p=1490863#post1490863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So basically there's a shadowlands, which is more or less ghostly twilight from cofd.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of. CoD's Twilight, as I understand it, is on the physical side of the gauntlet. WoD has the penumbras, which are the very shallow sides of the various umbras that tend to match well to the physical world. Since the Shroud has very similar mechanics to the Gauntlet, I tend to think of them as the same thing, which would make the Shadowlands a penumbra.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are these special gates which occasionally pop up in the shadowlands called nihils.<br /> Going into one leads you into some sorta underground memory-storm -ocean thing called The tempest.<br /> Now this tempest has a bunch of stable memory(?) islands which are home to the dark kingdoms*. </div> </div> </div>Home to the capital cities of the Dark Kingdoms, yes, but the Dark Kingdoms control areas in the Shadowlands. Stygia, the capital of the Dark Kingdom of Iron, is in the Tempest. The New York Necropolis, which is under control of the Dark Kingdom of Iron, is in the Shadowlands.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1489788-underworld-geography?p=1490865#post1490865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's pretty close. The Tempest is to the Shadowlands much like the Shadowlands are to the Skinlands - an extra dimension that overlaps them. The books use terms like 'below' to signify the distance from the Skinlands, which is more confusing than helpful imo, because they aren't really directional.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it helps, it's less about the Skinlands and more about Oblivion. Oblivion, as the great maw that everything falls into, tends to be thought of as down. The Tempest is 'below' the Shadowlands because it is 'closer' to Oblivion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Dark Kingdoms <i>are </i>Shadowlands. The Shadowlands are 'broken up' by the Tempest and 'Dark Kingdom' is just a label for a 'region' of the Shadowlands. That means if you want to move from one Necropolis to another, you would either have to go through the Tempest or use a Byway. </div> </div> </div>I can only partially agree with this, though. For every location in the Skinlands there should be a corresponding location in the Shadowlands. That includes very remote locations like mountaintops and the bottom of the ocean. Indeed it is quite possible for a Wraith to have a wrecked ship as a Fetter, so there really needs to be a Shadowlands location that matches to the Skinlands wreck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T05:08:59-07:00","id":1490985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1489788-underworld-geography?p=1490980#post1490980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can only partially agree with this, though. For every location in the Skinlands there should be a corresponding location in the Shadowlands. That includes very remote locations like mountaintops and the bottom of the ocean. Indeed it is quite possible for a Wraith to have a wrecked ship as a Fetter, so there really needs to be a Shadowlands location that matches to the Skinlands wreck.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, as I said: Lisbon to Beijing. But the books at times seem to imply that Tempest travel is mandatory to get from A to B - Wr20 books in particular. I like to think of it like the Shadowlands can indeed be mapped 1:1 to the Skinlands, but are also fractured by large swathes of Tempest leaking through.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T13:45:08-07:00","id":1491040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1489788-underworld-geography?p=1490985#post1490985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the books at times seem to imply that Tempest travel is mandatory to get from A to B - Wr20 books in particular.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd love to see any quotes that imply this. AFAIK, the Shadowlands exist everywhere throughout the Skinlands, and a ghost can walk through wilderness from point A to point B, unless the ST says otherwise.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T14:19:15-07:00","id":1491042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1489788-underworld-geography?p=1490913#post1490913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's one of those points that very much depends on how the ST wants to play it. Technically, you could walk in the Shadowlands from Lisbon to Beijing, but more likely than not you will be swallowed by a storm on the way and end up in the Tempest anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, serious question, but is this post not visible to others? I know the forum can act a bit dodgy at times.<br /> <br /> As for a quote, like I said, it's mostly implicit by how Tempest travel seems to be the preferred mode of travel. But the A to B quote is almost verbatim:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Book of Oblivion, p.45</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s important to understand that the Tempest connects places, and anybody who needs to get from Point A to Point B must cross it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T00:40:49-07:00","id":1491083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Callishka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1489788-underworld-geography?p=1491040#post1491040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd love to see any quotes that imply this. AFAIK, the Shadowlands exist everywhere throughout the Skinlands, and a ghost can walk through wilderness from point A to point B, unless the ST says otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd imagine places like West Europe being mostly mapped on the shadowlands due to pop-density but the further east you go, the more hazy is the reflection until you enter what would be the siberian wilderness but is in fact the tempest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27062-vampires-suck","name":"VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27062_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T06:53:47-07:00","id":1491089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1489788-underworld-geography?p=1491042#post1491042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh, serious question, but is this post not visible to others? I know the forum can act a bit dodgy at times.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the first post on its page and people generally start composing their response when they are on the previous page and aren't paying as much attention by the time they get to it. At least that's what happened to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for a quote, like I said, it's mostly implicit by how Tempest travel seems to be the preferred mode of travel. But the A to B quote is almost verbatim:<br /> </div> </div> </div>That book of Oblivion line is one of those that I treat more as defining the mood and feel of the Underworld rather than defining functionality. The first part, that the Tempest connects places, is true in almost every circumstance and its even the basis of Argos teleportation. The second part, that any path between point A and point B must pass through it, less so. That cannot function as a literal description of how things work, so it must be a figurative one.<br /> <br /> I'm actually not sure whether walking the Atlantic Ocean or braving the winds of the Tempest is the safer path between New York and London. Both sound like very good ways to get Harrowed. Byway travel is far safer, probably on par with hopping a plane, and though technically Byways pass through the Tempest I don't tend to categorize them as Tempest travel.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 08-23-2022, 10:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T12:19:21-07:00","id":1491112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1489788-underworld-geography?p=1491089#post1491089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the first post on its page and people generally start composing their response when they are on the previous page and aren't paying as much attention by the time they get to it. At least that's what happened to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I see, that makes sense. Thank you for verifying!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1489788-underworld-geography?p=1491089#post1491089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That book of Oblivion line is one of those that I treat more as defining the mood and feel of the Underworld rather than defining functionality. The first part, that the Tempest connects places, is true in almost every circumstance and its even the basis of Argos teleportation. The second part, that any path between point A and point B must pass through it, less so. That cannot function as a literal description of how things work, so it must be a figurative one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree! I think the emphasis on Tempest travel in the books stems from it being a mode of travel specific to the setting, whereas simply walking or driving in a relic vehicle is something players would have no problem to relate to. And I actually quite like the idea of extended Shadowland journeys, there are a lot of classic stories you can tell with travels through a wasteland.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1489788-underworld-geography?p=1491089#post1491089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually not sure whether walking the Atlantic Ocean or braving the winds of the Tempest is the safer path between New York and London. Both sound like very good ways to get Harrowed. Byway travel is far safer, probably on par with hopping a plane, and though technically Byways pass through the Tempest I don't tend to categorize them as Tempest travel.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't even know water was solid to Wraiths before reading it in Blood Dimmed Tides. Considering how thin the barrier between Shadowland ocean and the Tempest is (and what lurks in both of them), walking over open sea is probably more of a last resort option.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","